.TH KERN 1 "2025-11-30" "kern v1.2.3" "System Monitoring Tool"
.SH NAME
kern \- real-time system monitoring tool with TUI and REST API

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kern
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B kern
\fB\-a\fR | \fB\-\-all\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-c\fR | \fB\-\-cpu\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-d\fR | \fB\-\-disk\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-m\fR | \fB\-\-mem\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-n\fR | \fB\-\-net\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-g\fR | \fB\-\-gpu\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-\-ai\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-\-mining\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-r\fR [\fIPORT\fR] | \fB\-\-remote\fR [\fIPORT\fR]
.br
.B kern
\fB\-\-api\fR \fIURL\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-\-ssh\fR \fIHOST\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kern
is a comprehensive system monitoring tool that provides real-time information 
about system resources including disk usage, CPU performance, memory utilization, 
network statistics, GPU metrics, AI training processes, and cryptocurrency mining activity.

The tool features a professional Terminal User Interface (TUI) with double buffering
to eliminate screen flickering, support for multiple languages with automatic download 
capability, and multi-protocol remote monitoring via HTTP, HTTPS, and SSH.

.B kern
automatically starts a background API server on port 28126 during installation, 
providing immediate access to monitoring data via REST API without any manual configuration.

.B kern
remembers your last used monitoring modules and will automatically show them when run without arguments.

.SH PLATFORMS
.B kern
supports the following platforms:

.B Linux:
AMD64, ARM64, ARMv7 architectures

.B macOS:  
Intel and Apple Silicon (AMD64, ARM64)

.B Windows:
AMD64 architecture

