.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Show all system information. This is the default behavior on first run.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cpu
Show CPU information only, including model, cores, threads, usage percentage, frequency, and load averages.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-disk
Show disk information only, including filesystem type, size, usage, and mount points.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mem
Show memory information only, including RAM and swap usage with visual graphs.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-net
Show network information only, including interface status, IP/MAC addresses, and traffic statistics.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-gpu
Show GPU information only. Requires NVIDIA drivers (nvidia-smi) or AMD ROCm (rocm-smi).
.TP
.B \-\-ai
Show AI training information only, including framework detection, VRAM usage, and training metrics.
.TP
.B \-\-mining
Show cryptocurrency mining information only, including algorithm, hashrate, and efficiency metrics.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information and application logo.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show comprehensive help message.
.TP
.BI \-\-refresh= SECONDS
Set refresh interval in seconds. Default is 2 seconds. Minimum is 1 second.
.TP
.BI \-l " LANG" "\fR, " \-\-lang " LANG"
Set interface language. Language pack must be downloaded first using \fB\-\-download-lang\fR. Use \fB\-\-list-languages\fR to see all supported codes.
.TP
.BI \-r " [PORT]" "\fR, " \-\-remote " [PORT]"
Start remote API server on specified port. Default port is 28126 if not specified.
.TP
.BR \-\-detailed ", " \-de
Show detailed CPU core information including individual core usage percentages. This setting is not persisted between sessions.
.TP
.BR \-\-detailed-mem ", " \-dm
Show detailed memory module information including slot, size, type, speed, and usage percentages. This setting is not persisted between sessions.
.TP
.BI \-\-api " URL"
Monitor remote server via HTTP/HTTPS API. URL should be in format http://host:port or https://host:port.
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh " HOST"
Monitor remote server via SSH. Format should be user@hostname.
.TP
.BI \-\-download-lang " CODE"
Download language pack for specified language code.
.TP
.B \-\-list-languages
List all supported language codes.
.TP
.B \-\-logo
Show application logo during monitoring.
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Start kern as a daemon service.
.TP
.B \-\-start-service
Start the kern daemon service.
.TP
.B \-\-stop-service
Stop the kern daemon service.
.TP
.B \-\-restart-service
Restart the kern daemon service.
.TP
.B \-\-service-status
Show daemon service status.
.TP
.B \-\-enable-service
Enable auto-start on system boot.
.TP
.B \-\-disable-service
Disable auto-start on system boot.
.TP
.B \-\-ensure-running
Ensure daemon service is running.
.TP
.BI \-\-remote-port " PORT"
Start API server on custom port (used with \-\-remote).

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B kern
Show all system information using smart defaults (remembers last used modules).
.TP
.B kern --cpu --mem
Show only CPU and memory information.
.TP
.B kern --gpu --ai
Show GPU and AI training information.
.TP
.B kern --mining
Show cryptocurrency mining information.
.TP
.B kern -d -l ru
Show disk information with Russian interface.
.TP
.B kern --refresh=5
Update display every 5 seconds.
.TP
.B kern --detailed
Show detailed CPU core usage information.
.TP
.B kern -r
Start API server on default port 28126.
.TP
.B kern --remote-port 8080
Start API server on port 8080.
.TP
.B kern --api http://192.168.1.100:28126
Monitor remote server via HTTP API.
.TP
.B kern --api https://monitor.example.com:28126
Monitor remote server via HTTPS API.
.TP
.B kern --ssh user@hostname
Monitor remote server via SSH.
.TP
.B kern --download-lang fr
Download French language pack.
.TP
.B kern --start-service
Start kern daemon service.
.TP
.B kern --service-status
Check daemon service status.

